#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572777} :activity/id #uuid "2c29e55b-b341-52a9-b493-b94632920cac" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049788 :topic/id #uuid "1420f0fa-c9b8-5cba-8bba-e14cbf53c041" :topic/math-academy-id 1776} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572735 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120458 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cce91bb-3f2d-594d-b001-b74e585728b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327044} {:answer/id #uuid "37c36c30-f71a-5c42-8e1f-9edf8e05698a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327418} {:answer/id #uuid "44045eca-a7ba-59e9-8fbf-163cca4eb93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327529} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8f6fbd-305a-5b73-bdfc-0528e914b0e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328994} {:answer/id #uuid "f06bdfa7-6d66-5967-9f0e-3a7302aa595b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329032}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329032} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa8ff1ea-d3d8-5891-8607-26ac9e965d86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d9b84023-6745-5aae-a304-bc4f9a263b31" :question/math-academy-id "q-43113" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+2z &=6 \\\\ 3x+2y-z &=k \\\\ 4x+3y-3z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that $x=1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-9,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ k & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-6+3)+(-3k+1)+2(3k-2) \\\\  & =-18-3k+1+6k-4 \\\\  & =3k-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{3k-21}{-9}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-9}{3k-21} & =1 \\\\ -9 & =3k-21 \\\\ 12 & =3k \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "127f1300-1391-54f6-9fe2-9e7626e9b022" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572803}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572744 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a6e5ce-0937-5891-acbd-fe85f7b69928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269454} {:answer/id #uuid "210764b5-81bd-5952-a203-b8566ae3024c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269549} {:answer/id #uuid "2dbb50f3-7690-5e1c-a197-81d54236aeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269680} {:answer/id #uuid "9f609c62-980b-5132-960e-b964150a53e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270684} {:answer/id #uuid "cbfc859d-6747-5db9-9c26-4254f83b9a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271060}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186270684} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c4e3630-6513-56c7-9a3b-beeebecf2727" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1e8e68a9-7d99-5bc1-967a-dd0267847130" :question/math-academy-id "q-139989" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y-2z &=-7 \\\\ 2x+y-4z &=-10 \\\\ 3x-3y-2z &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $16,$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+(-5)y+(-2z) &=-7 \\\\ 2x+1y+(-4)z &=-10 \\\\ 3x+(-3)y+(-2)z &=-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ -3 & -7\\end{aligned}|-(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{aligned}|+(-7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-7-30)+5(-14+30)-7(-6-3) \\\\  & =-111+80+63 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{32}{16}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2c72979c-0908-5fbd-85a9-ea945295a125" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572753}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572753 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "347efb70-e44d-50c1-be1b-19ddcd858876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269749} {:answer/id #uuid "3dcf7c57-596b-56d8-bbc4-4ef2fd738db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269833} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa92296-a8c7-5064-987e-0dba2a5c3ade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270381} {:answer/id #uuid "9fe23528-de1b-5e36-a053-630ae11946e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270690} {:answer/id #uuid "e42035ba-5a21-54af-b741-93298da3d242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271278}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269833} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5425c9e-f9a3-50d1-b38c-a404e2f613e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b99085c9-ade3-5f37-a123-f7c001cf1137" :question/math-academy-id "q-140042" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y-5z &=1 \\\\ 2x+3y-3z &=k \\\\ -5x+3y+7z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that $y=-1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-19,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|=-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -3 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}|+(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(7k-6)-(14-15)-5(-4+5k) \\\\  & =21k-18+1+20-25k \\\\  & =-4k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{-4k+3}{-19}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=-1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4k+3}{-19} & =-1 \\\\ -4k+3 & =19 \\\\ -4k & =16 \\\\ k & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3d43bf3e-2fb8-5456-b231-9a491908f785"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572777 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329710 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f3c771f-c51e-5841-8533-1a9671c2d6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327488} {:answer/id #uuid "596aae9d-1263-5f81-8c32-fcfac678f572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327717} {:answer/id #uuid "ac1518da-c8dd-5fdb-b4cb-d1e5e1748f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328428} {:answer/id #uuid "f915f45d-2c74-53be-8b2d-4264b352acb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329119} {:answer/id #uuid "fea619bf-5465-56b2-9f3c-9d1185630620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329170} :answer-field/id #uuid "21719854-d3df-595d-91dc-6df416673b0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "205fc41d-e809-53d1-80b0-a8abf73a7907" :question/math-academy-id "q-43108" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z &=1 \\\\ 5x+3y+4z &=2 \\\\ x+y-z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-1,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+1z &=1 \\\\ 5x+3y+4z &=2 \\\\ 1x+1y+(-1)z &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3-4)-2(-2-4)+(2-3) \\\\  & =-7+12-1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{4}{-1}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "85a99d67-08c7-5c39-919b-70a7c169d796" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572735}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572803 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e0253b-532c-58d8-b091-347993c3f893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416273} {:answer/id #uuid "061ca3b9-19da-5830-8387-482e73317df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416274} {:answer/id #uuid "489fa8d1-175b-5fa4-8798-bbe1b2637681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416279} {:answer/id #uuid "73c24e43-321d-50e6-b1e7-cdf2748817be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416283} {:answer/id #uuid "b917f57a-83ba-5e72-bb47-0cffe8883bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416290}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416274} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc965890-90b8-58cc-bc3f-efeb4ad8684c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2a3030e8-5052-55cf-b8fe-d458398f5913" :question/math-academy-id "q-73691" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-3y &=1 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z &=0 \\\\ y-z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-21,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+(-3)y+0z &=1 \\\\ 5x+4y+(-2)z &=0 \\\\ 0x+1y+(-1)z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{y},$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the second column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(0+6)-(-5-0)+0 \\\\  & =18+5 \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{23}{-21}=-\\frac{23}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "eda35098-d403-5441-92fc-05e024fcafb1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572744}}] :activity/title "Cramer’s Rule for 3x3 Systems" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572299}]}
